+.TH BRIGHTERY-DOCTOR 1 "November 2026" "Brightery Doctor 1.2.0" "User Commands"
+.SH NAME
+brightery-doctor \- read-only Linux server health dashboard
+.SH SYNOPSIS
+.B brightery-doctor
+.RI [ OPTIONS ]
+.SH DESCRIPTION
+.B brightery-doctor
+samples Linux CPU activity, memory availability, I/O pressure,
+disk activity, and process states to help identify possible
+performance bottlenecks. It displays a terminal dashboard with
+green (healthy), amber (warning), or red (critical) status indicators.
+It can also produce offline HTML and machine-readable JSON reports.
+.PP
+The diagnostic scan is read-only. It does not open a network port,
+change permissions, restart services, or install packages.
+Only the explicitly requested report files may be written.
+The findings are heuristic and do not establish a root cause.
+.SH OPTIONS
+.TP
+.B \-\-seconds SECONDS
+Duration of the sample, from 1 to 120 seconds. Default: 6 seconds.
+.TP
+.B \-\-interval SECONDS
+Sampling interval, from 0.5 to 5 seconds. Default: 1 second.
+.TP
+.B \-\-json
+Print structured JSON instead of the terminal dashboard.
+.TP
+.B \-\-plain
+Print the legacy plain-text diagnostic output.
+.TP
+.B \-\-color
+Force ANSI dashboard coloring, even when standard output is redirected.
+.TP
+.B \-\-no\-color
+Disable ANSI dashboard colors.
+.TP
+.B \-\-ascii
+Use ASCII borders rather than Unicode box-drawing characters.
+.TP
+.B \-\-save FILE
+Create a new JSON report file with permissions 0600.
+Existing destination files are not overwritten.
+.TP
+.B \-\-report FILE
+Create a new, color-free text report with permissions 0600.
+Existing destination files are not overwritten.
+.TP
+.B \-\-html\-report FILE
+Create a new, self-contained, offline HTML report with permissions 0600.
+No external assets, scripts, or listening services are required.
+Existing destination files are not overwritten.
+.TP
+.B \-\-include\-hostname
+Include the host name in generated report data.
+The host name is omitted by default.
+.TP
+.B \-\-version
+Print the application version and exit.
+.TP
+.B \-h, \-\-help
+Print command-line help and exit.
+.SH EXAMPLES
+.TP
+.B brightery-doctor
+Scan and display the default terminal dashboard.
+.TP
+.B brightery-doctor \-\-seconds 15
+Collect a longer sample.
+.TP
+.B brightery-doctor \-\-json
+Write a JSON report to standard output.
+.TP
+.B brightery-doctor \-\-html\-report /tmp/server-health.html
+Create an offline HTML report that can be opened in a browser.
+.SH SECURITY AND PRIVACY
+The process command-line arguments are not retained in reports.
+Only a limited portion of command-line data is inspected to detect
+recursive permission operations. Reports may include process names,
+process IDs, and service names; review them before sharing.
+.PP
+Report files are created with mode 0600 and are not overwritten.
+Choose a trusted parent directory for sensitive reports.
+.SH LIMITATIONS
+Results describe a bounded observation window. A healthy result
+does not prove an absence of problems outside that window.
+Measurement availability and performance thresholds vary by system.
+.SH AUTHOR
+Brightery <support@brightery.com>
+.SH SEE ALSO
+.BR proc (5),
+.BR iostat (1),
+.BR top (1)
